    {{#> expert-feature }}
        <h2>Does Micro-Infusion hurt?</h2>
        <article>
            <p>Qure Micro-Infusion is designed to be virtually painless. Its tiny, 0.5 mm gold-plated microneedles gently stamp the skin, unlike more aggressive treatments that involve rolling or dragging.</p>
            <p>You may feel a slight prickling, similar to Velcro lightly pressed against your skin. As you stamp, the tiny microneedles create channels that help your skin absorb Qure's serum for smoother-looking, more radiant skin.</p>
        </article>
        <div class="expert-card">
            <blockquote>"What I really like about Qure Micro-Infusion is the thought put into safe at-home use. Every treatment starts with a fresh, sterile, single-use needle head. That attention to detail matters."</blockquote>
            <div class="expert-card__author">
                <div>
                    <span>Dr. Shah</span>
                    <small>1.2M followers</small>
                </div>
                <div class="e-pill-badge e-pill-badge--xs">Board Certified Dermatologist</div>
            </div>
            <picture>
